From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a window is black until its page draws

Until a page's first frame, a window shows kColorWebContentsBackground:
Chrome's new-tab background, white in a light theme and gray in a dark
one. On a tty the shell window showed it between the boot screen and
the shell's first frame, a white flash on every start (#2467). The
engine has no new-tab page, so it is black.

Verified: reproduced on the pinned engine nested in a headless sway; a
theme whose new-tab background is blue turned the flash blue. Not
built here; the engine job builds it on crux.
---
 chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixer.cc | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixer.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixer.cc
index 8e3c1d6..0095079 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixer.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_mixer.cc
@@ -862,8 +862,9 @@ void AddChromeColorMixer(ui::ColorProvider* provider,
       GetToolbarTopSeparatorColorTransform(kColorToolbar,
                                            ui::kColorFrameInactive);
   mixer[kColorSettingsWebuiPageBackground] = {ui::kColorSysSurface2};
-  mixer[kColorWebContentsBackground] =
-      ui::SetAlpha(kColorNewTabPageBackground, SK_AlphaOPAQUE);
+  // Domicile: a window shows this until its page's first frame. There is no
+  // new-tab page, so it is black, as the screen is before the desktop starts.
+  mixer[kColorWebContentsBackground] = {SK_ColorBLACK};
   mixer[kColorWebContentsBackgroundLetterboxing] =
       ui::AlphaBlend(kColorWebContentsBackground, SK_ColorBLACK, 0x33);
   mixer[kColorWindowControlButtonBackgroundActive] = {ui::kColorFrameActive};
